  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Knowledge Broker to Support the Climate Adaptation and Resilience (CLARE) Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Research for Impact (R4I Hub), hosted by SouthSouthNorth, uses a knowledge brokering approach to support the CLARE programme to build capacity and directly deliver on long term impact to ensure knowledge and evidence generated are taken up and used/actioned to increase the resilience of vulnerable communities. The objectives are to: &#x2022;Support research for impact objectives within the CLARE research projects through strengthening their knowledge brokering capacities;&#x2022;Broker existing knowledge from CLARE and predecessor programmes;&#x2022;Support to CLARE learning on research for impact and sharing emerging CLARE lessons; and &#x2022;Amplifying CLARE knowledge and evidence into high level policy processes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="XM-DAC-301-2" role="1" type="15">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Canada - International Development Research Centre/Centre de recherches pour le d&#xE9;veloppement international</narrative>
